    "method": "Re-run: tiktoken.get_encoding(name) for cl100k_base, o200k_base, p50k_base; for each pair in manifest.test_set compute len(encode(ainglish)) - len(encode(english)); take the per-tokenizer mean; headline value is the MAXIMUM mean across the three (least favourable tokenizer), value_lo/value_hi are min/max across them. Equivalent to ainglish.measure.token_delta(pairs, tokenizers)['floor']. Stimuli are derived mechanically from this proposal's own served canonical templates - 'In <S>, start no new tasks; let running tasks finish.' / 'In <S>, start no new tasks; interrupt running tasks.' against 'Stop <S>, finish-started.' / 'Stop <S>, interrupt-started.' - with <S> substituted unchanged, 32 bounded task-instance sets over the four declared domains (downloads, print jobs, exports, analysis batches), each set yielding one pair per form: 64 pairs, 32 per form. No teaching paragraph was added to the English arm, both English clauses are present on every item, and no long machine label appears on one side only; the only difference between arms within a pair is the template. S is held unchanged across arms as the construct requires, so the set name cancels exactly and the per-pair delta is constant within a form (-6 finish-started, -5 interrupt-started on all three tokenizers, 32/32 pairs each). The declared 64 pairs therefore contain 2 distinct delta values in total, not 64; the pair count is nominal and no bank-derived sampling uncertainty exists. This is a template-level deterministic comparison. DECLARED COSTS (this proposal requires them reported separately): one-time entry cost, taken as the token count of the served canonical mapping text - {'cl100k_base': 45, 'o200k_base': 47, 'p50k_base': 48} tokens across the three tokenizers; repeated-use break-even = ceil(entry/|saving per use|) = {'cl100k_base': 9, 'o200k_base': 9, 'p50k_base': 9} uses. Not hidden inside an assumed amortisation count.",
